From: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sprd: advertise the rate the converter is fixed to

A board that sets fixed-sample-rate in DT pins the codec's converters to
that rate: sprd_codec_pcm_hw_params() throws params_rate() away and
programs the fixed value instead. Nothing resamples for it, because the
AP path's SRC is programmed for capture only:

  static bool ap_ad_src_check(int scene_id, int stream)
  {
  	if (stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE &&
  		scene_id == VBC_DAI_ID_NORMAL_AP01)
  		return true;
  	return false;
  }

codec_reconfig_dai_rate() nevertheless answers SNDRV_PCM_RATE_CONTINUOUS
for such a board, so the DAI claims every rate it will in fact refuse to
honour. Android never noticed - its HAL only ever opens the fixed rate -
but any userspace that trusts the advertised range gets a stream played
out at the converter's speed instead of its own. On RG Rotate, whose DT
has fixed-sample-rate = <48000 48000 48000>, requesting 32 kHz plays
1.5x fast and 96 kHz plays an octave down, with no error anywhere:

  [ASoC:SC2730] Playback rate is [48000], ivsence_dmic_type 0
  [ASoC: VBC ] scene_normal_hw_params: data_fmt=VBC_DAT_L16, chan=2, rate =32000

Advertise the fixed rate and only the fixed rate, and let the core
resample into it. The rate that is actually programmed does not change.

Reporting it is not enough on its own: the sprd card builds its frontends
without dpcm_merged_rate, so a backend's rate constraint never reaches the
PCM userspace opens, and hw:0,0 kept offering 8000-192000 however narrow
the codec behind it was. Merge it for the dynamic links.

Signed-off-by: Tomonori Nakagawa <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
DISABLED: correct as an analysis but not needed here, and it narrows what the
DAI advertises for every board in the family rather than just this one. On RG
Rotate nothing asks for a rate other than 48 kHz: the WirePlumber rules the
board ships pin PipeWire to S16LE/48000, and the UCM profile points plain ALSA
users at the same front end. Kept for the explanation of why a mismatched rate
plays at the converter's speed with no error reported anywhere, which is worth
having written down if another ums512 board turns up without those rules.
diff --git a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-asoc-card-utils.c b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-asoc-card-utils.c
index cba59647bf0b..e4ec1f1af65c 100755
--- a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-asoc-card-utils.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-asoc-card-utils.c
@@ -285,6 +285,15 @@ static int asoc_sprd_card_dai_link_of_misc(struct device_node *node,
 		dai_link->dynamic = !!val[0];
 	pr_debug("%s dynamic: %u\n", __func__, dai_link->dynamic);
 
+	/*
+	 * A frontend that does not merge its backends' rate constraint
+	 * advertises the raw FE range (8k-192k continuous) whatever the
+	 * codec behind it can actually do, and userspace picks a rate the
+	 * hardware then silently ignores.
+	 */
+	if (dai_link->dynamic)
+		dai_link->dpcm_merged_rate = 1;
+
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(node, "no-pcm", val);
 	if (ret) {
 		if (ret != -EINVAL)
diff --git a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c
index d32459d9a1e4..92cec59f5f5b 100755
--- a/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sprd/vendor/sprd-codec.c
@@ -3855,19 +3855,35 @@ static void codec_reconfig_dai_rate(struct snd_soc_component *codec)
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * If fixed_rates is provided, tell user that this codec supports
-	 * all kinds of rates.
+	 * If fixed_rates is provided, the converter runs at that rate and
+	 * nothing else: sprd_codec_pcm_hw_params() discards params_rate()
+	 * in favour of it, and the AP playback path has no SRC to make up
+	 * the difference (ap_hw_params() only programs one for capture).
+	 * Advertise the fixed rate alone so the core resamples for us -
+	 * claiming SNDRV_PCM_RATE_CONTINUOUS here let any other rate be
+	 * accepted and then played back at the converter's speed.
 	 */
 	list_for_each_entry(dai, &codec->dai_list, list) {
-		if (fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_DA])
-			dai->driver->playback.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_CONTINUOUS;
-		if ((dai->driver->id == SPRD_CODEC_IIS0_ID &&
-		     fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_AD]) ||
-		    (dai->driver->id != SPRD_CODEC_IIS0_ID &&
-		     fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_AD1]))
-			dai->driver->capture.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_CONTINUOUS;
-		else
+		unsigned int ad_fixed =
+			(dai->driver->id == SPRD_CODEC_IIS0_ID) ?
+			fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_AD] : fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_AD1];
+
+		if (fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_DA]) {
+			dai->driver->playback.rates = snd_pcm_rate_to_rate_bit(
+				fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_DA]);
+			dai->driver->playback.rate_min =
+				fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_DA];
+			dai->driver->playback.rate_max =
+				fixed_rates[CODEC_PATH_DA];
+		}
+		if (ad_fixed) {
+			dai->driver->capture.rates =
+				snd_pcm_rate_to_rate_bit(ad_fixed);
+			dai->driver->capture.rate_min = ad_fixed;
+			dai->driver->capture.rate_max = ad_fixed;
+		} else {
 			dai->driver->capture.rates &= ~unsupported_rates;
+		}
 	}
 }
 
